This is a pretty solid RPG, with a fun storyline, although it might not fit everyone's tastes. If you have already played Gothic, Gothic 2 or Risen, you will know exactly what to expect from Risen 2: you are going to play a cynical backstabber who will save quite a few people for purely selfish reasons.
Improvements:
- the game is more ambitious;
- the graphics have improved considerably;
- the storyline is funnier;
- magic is pretty original;
- treasure hunting;
- dirty tricks (i.e. launching sand or salt in the opponent's eyes, or even a parrot).
Unchanged:
- in the start, you will die a lot;
- rather unbalanced action-combat;
- lots of backstabbing and stealing from people :)
Anyway, I just finished the game and I'm giving myself a few weeks before I start Risen 3 :)

